 "section_summary": "This section contains two State Department cover despatches from the U.S. Political Adviser for Japan in Tokyo (dated May 25 and June 10, 1948) transmitting Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers (SCAP) Civil Information and Education Section research reports on Japanese educational institutions. The primary document is Part 24 of a nationwide survey, focusing on Miyagi Prefecture, which provides statistical tables and detailed rosters of schools as of April and November 1946. The material outlines institutional administration, enrollment figures by gender, and faculty numbers across various levels of schooling, including universities, colleges, normal schools, secondary and vocational schools, youth schools, and elementary institutions under national, prefectural, municipal, and town or village control.",
