   "summary": "This special report compiles administrative and statistical data on educational institutions across Miyagi Prefecture as of April and November 1946, prior to the postwar reorganization of Japan's school system. Introductory sections analyze the administrative control structure, school types, and historical data limitations, followed by summary statistical tables showing student enrollment and teacher numbers broken down by gender, school level, and jurisdictional control. The roster section lists individual institutions—including Tohoku Imperial University, colleges, normal schools, secondary and middle schools, vocational institutes, and youth schools—providing foundation dates, locations, enrollments, and faculty counts.",
